INTERPRETATION
For d=K-1-2Q from four through nine, the analyzer uses the normalized
full/partial/empty packet partition of Lemma 5A8H28M.  On every
stable ray and cone it reconstructs the exact degree-at-most-eight
Newton polynomial, rejects a negative coefficient, and rejects a
nonzero ninth difference.  The finite boundary entries are exhaustive.
Thus each command is an unbounded proof in Q for its fixed d, not a
bounded sign scan.  The increasing number of negative odd packets
confirms that the even reserve is essential.

